{"kind":"propose","text":"S6 item 3 proposes Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups on the HTML for /oauth/authorize, matching the tested /page policy. Consent validates the existing OAuth context and returns through location.assign. Room source does not read window.opener or use postMessage. A cross-origin client that opens this route with an incompatible opener policy can lose its opener link under HTML's COOP matching rules. Authorize that browser behavior, or direct a different compatibility choice before the source changes. A local red/green route test will check the response header. A scripted local browser fixture can demonstrate callback navigation and the opener boundary without a provider.\n\nThe Site assessment requested by S6 and review 79daff0f is separate. Current Site HTML supports same-tab links, same-origin routed images, HTTPS/data images, inline styles and raw attachments. Its current policy excludes framing, forms and scripts. Standards analysis predicts ordinary same-tab navigation and img-src 'self' will still work with a bare CSP sandbox, and predicts a sandbox download restriction. The current attachment response itself already carries sandbox, so a browser comparison is necessary to establish whether applying it to HTML changes actual download behavior. No Site policy change is proposed. See https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#cross-origin-opener-policies, https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#allowed-to-navigate, https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#parse-response and https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#directive-sandbox.","body":{"to":"planner"}}